  "conclusion": "Candidate 798 contains the roof complex of the 2409 estate. Centre and outline confirm the red-roof group rather than the main hotel. Modern surveys clearly separate a northern branched group with eastern transverse roof and a second crosswing south of it, connected by a narrower portion. The old main facade may be compared with the northern/eastern multi-roof front, but sources to date do not prove a one-to-one historic identity for every roof or the original farm/garage/ancillary wings. Retain the ordinary footprint in full until sufficient physical correspondence permits local registration.",
